  "result": "I've written the revised record for `NRS_484B_777_1_o1` to `record.jsonl` in the repair directory. It hasn't been checked yet: the harness validates it next, then the coder rewrites the rule and runs the gate.\n\nThe gate refused the rule because the left-turn exception (b) checked for an intersection `i` or a driveway entrance `d` anywhere in the scene, with nothing tying it to the rider. The record now ties it, and fixes two problems in the planned scenarios:\n\n1. **Left-turn exception (b) is now tied to the rider.** I added an element on span `s5`. The declared left turn now counts only at an intersection or driveway/alley entrance that lies on the same highway as the roadway the rider occupies. A left turn off that roadway can only be made where its way meets another, so this doesn't narrow the exception. I've put that argument in the element's justification. No distance limit is added.\n   - Span `s2` now maps only to `rel.occupies` and `st.roadway`, the same as the sibling node `_o2`. The intersection and entrance atoms moved to `s5`.\n   - This is the tie the coder tried in their diagnostic run. With it, the gate passed this check and reached the witness tests.\n\n2. **`branch_1` to `branch_4` now expect `not_applicable`, not `compliant`.** In each of them an exception holds, and the record says the duty doesn't apply when one does. I also reworded `branch_1`, whose description contradicted itself.\n\n3. **The old `branch_5` (the electric scooter) is dropped.** In the current reading, the electric-scooter group doesn't count the plain `ru.electric_scooter` class as a confirmed member. So no scooter can be confirmed as a subject, and that scene could only ever come out `unknown`. As a result, no scenario tests the lawful-speed check that comes from `NRS_484B_785_1a`, because that check only matters for scooters. Fixing that needs a change to how the scooter group is read, which this node can't make.\n\n4. **A new `branch_5` (expects `violated`) tests the new tie.** It is the `forbid` scene with a left turn declared at an intersection on a different highway. Because that turn doesn't count, the duty still applies and is broken.\n\nThe other spans' mappings, the applicability and duty texts other than exception (b), the parameters and the narrowings are unchanged.",
